#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:5 ee792640e0714af68891f9f2a3bd4e70
msgid "Basic Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:7 f07a598dcd024d318fcbd309df3dbc1c
msgid "this page superseded and is now ARCHIVED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:9 1c1e4e63f97f4aedb4b503ec9bdee28a
msgid "This topic covers basic Roll and pitch and throttle tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:12 6a1516cf1a394d8691829770b29dbb8f
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:14 9d3ad6c37b494b57b79cb1853887a023
msgid ""
"After your first flight, you may notice that you copter doesn't respond "
"to control inputs the way you want it to or you may have trouble "
"maintaining control of your copter. If you are familiar with PID "
"controllers, check out the :ref:`advanced tuning guide here <tuning>`. If"
" you are an experienced operator, try out :ref:`the autotune feature "
"<autotune>`. This page will cover the basic tuning section of Mission "
"Planner and APM Planner that simplified the complex tuning process into a"
" few simple sliders. This is the best tuning method for new operators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:24 4695c08976204fafb34b9f7457083f73
msgid "Roll and pitch tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:26 bbf3bb20f4fb400db0938c51576231ae
msgid ""
"Tuning is easiest at the field using a :ref:`telemetry radio <common-"
"telemetry-landingpage>`. Perform an initial flight with the following "
"questions in mind:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:29 063d9461a4d042a3ad68b7db50e193f7
msgid ""
"How does the copter respond to roll and pitch? Is the response more "
"sluggish or twitchy than you want?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:31 d49b2694b0ab43f3a756ff8dba98beee
msgid ""
"When the copter is hover, what level is the throttle set at? Does it "
"hover at the middle position of the stick or is it above or below the "
"center position?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:34 f55831396d604594ab0271634d0e5391
msgid ""
"When raising the throttle, what rate does the copter accelerate at? Does "
"it gain altitude more slowly or more quickly than you want?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:37 b4b1dce332724028aeccb920532376bb
msgid ""
"Connect the telemetry radio ground module to your ground station computer"
" and open either Mission Planner or APM Planner. Select the correct COM "
"port and select Connect. You should see live data on the Flight Data "
"screen. To begin tuning, select Config/Tuning and Basic Tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:43 b7783e6e1ec944edbdf4f5cc8a0457f6
msgid ""
"Start with the Roll/Pitch slider at the top of the page. If you observed "
"that your copter was too twitchy in response to roll and pitch controls, "
"move the slider one tick mark to the left, or, if you observed that your "
"copter was too sluggish, move the slider one tick mark to the right. "
"Repeat your flight to determine if the change was beneficial. Repeat the "
"process until you are satisfied with the way your copter responds to roll"
" and pitch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:58 bc432a24ca3945cda95537fcb8b62779
msgid "Throttle tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:60 decd9d3a626941f48723fd4f03c92113
msgid ""
"The bottom two sliders allows you to tune the throttle control. Adjust "
"the slider marked Throttle Hover until the copter hovers at the throttle "
"stick's middle position. If the copter hovers with the throttle stick "
"above middle position, move the slider to the left by one tick-mark until"
" it hovers at mid-stick, testing as you go. If the copter hovers with the"
" throttle stick below middle position, move the slider to the right by "
"single tick-mark increments until it does. Make sure to test each set of "
"tuning settings as you go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:69 329e1bd32dfb4fc6b91ce646064b3a04
msgid ""
"Move the slider marked Throttle Accel or Climb Sensitivity to the right "
"to have the copter gain altitude more aggressively or to the left to have"
" the copter gain altitude more gently. Test each increment after setting "
"to evaluate the tune."
msgstr ""

